zlibcomplete
------------------------------------------
C++ interface to the ZLib library supporting compression with FLUSH,
decompression, and std::string. RAII

Runtime requirements:
  cygwin-3.6.12-1
  libgcc1-14.4.0-1
  libstdc++6-14.4.0-1
  libzlibcomplete-devel-1.0.5-1bl3
  libzlibcomplete0-1.0.5-1bl3
  pkg-config-3.0.11-1
  zlib-devel-1.4-1
  zlib0-1.4-1

Build requirements:
(besides corresponding -devel packages)
  binutils-2.47-1
  cmake-4.4.5-1
  cygport-0.37.13-1
  gcc-g++-14.4.0-1
  ninja-1.13.2-1
  ruby-4.0.9-1
  zlib-devel-1.4-1

Canonical website:
  https://github.com/rudi-cilibrasi/zlibcomplete

Canonical download:
  https://github.com/rudi-cilibrasi/zlibcomplete/archive/refs/tags/1.0.5.tar.gz

-------------------------------------------

Build instructions:
  1. unpack zlibcomplete-1.0.5-X-src.tar.xz
  2. if you use setup to install this src package,
     it will be unpacked under /usr/src automatically
        % cd /usr/src
        % cygport ./zlibcomplete-1.0.5-X.cygport all

This will create:
  /usr/src/zlibcomplete-1.0.5-X-src.tar.xz
  /usr/src/zlibcomplete-1.0.5-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libzlibcomplete0-1.0.5-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libzlibcomplete-devel-1.0.5-X.tar.xz

-------------------------------------------

